What role are you?
If archaeologist, I suspect you'd do more damage with a mattock than
Snickersnee, although you'd have to look it up.  Otherwise ditch the
mattock for a pickaxe.
I'd wear the robe (MC3) rather than the [oDisp (only MC2).
Displacement isn't all that important, especially with intrinsic
invisibility.

If you can cast create monster reliably it might be worth some more
sac-and-pray antics until you get a bit more protection.
To be honest, I'd wear polycontrol to protect my armour from polytraps
and just keep exploring deeper.  You're going to need to get to XL 14
somehow anyway, and you might as well be picking up items from the
dungeon floor and monster drops as you do it.

One thing you do need is an escape item.  Wearing telecontrol and
having a c?oT is great, if you have the spare food to burn two ring
hungers; casting create monster can get you food too, I guess,
although it burns some nutrition on the way.
Stash the other 3 rings, and spare magical armour at the altar and
come back once you've found a /oPoly.
If you can #twoweapon it may be worth ditching the shield for a long
sword / katana / silver sabre - but only twoweapon easy monsters until
you get it to basic (happens fast enough).

Sticking the first uncursed elf hat you find on your head will help
lower spell failure rates (compared with a metal helm) if that's an
issue.

Good luck!
